# The ruling: "If the target Equipment can't legally be attached to the target attacking creature when Raubahn's last ability
# resolves, the Equipment won't move." Turn 3: Raubahn and Ornithopter attack and the trigger targets the white Stormbeacon Blade
# and the Ornithopter (Raubahn is red, so the Ornithopter is a legal target). In response Mother of Runes gives the Ornithopter
# protection from white: the Blade, a white source, cannot be attached to it (CR 702.16d, 701.3b), so it stays unattached and
# the Ornithopter is a 0/2. Both targets are still legal (CR 608.2b), the ability resolves, and Bot2 takes only Raubahn's 2.
# The first Raubahn scenario is the control: with no protection the same trigger attaches the Equipment.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo
Mother of Runes
Stormbeacon Blade
Ornithopter
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Close mana window)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stormbeacon Blade.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Stormbeacon Blade)
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Activate(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Colors(White)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
? Stack.Count = 0
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Life = 18

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Stormbeacon Blade.AttachedTo = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Raubahn, Bull of Ala Mhigo.Power = 2
